That was the first time that something like that ever happened to me on the court.

00:03:35.632 --> 00:03:39.093
And I just, I guess it just relaxed me a bit as I thought about it because

00:03:39.093 --> 00:03:41.346
I’m like, “Man, I been through everything, and this is another

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:43.056
—something else that I gotta get over, so—”

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:43.514
- Yeah.

00:03:43.514 --> 00:03:46.226
- “Let me get my ass up, walk to the locker room and figure out what’s next.”

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:48.770
- But you know what happened, right? So when you were down, 

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.688
and then I stole the ball on that play,

00:03:50.688 --> 00:03:53.608
but in my head, it was like, you fell down and you just lost your shoes.-

00:03:53.608 --> 00:03:54.442
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. It was—

00:03:54.442 --> 00:03:55.485
